        "notes": "Reads the notes ref's history (merges skipped; each side's commits carry their versions). A remove and an add of the same note in one notes commit is git reorganising the notes tree into fan-out directories, not a change, and is folded (git-gud's review found phantom 'removed' entries past ~256 notes; tested with 300). Restoring a wip version carries it line by line onto the current snapshot, or copies it as is with a warning if its snapshot is gone."
      },
