    "risks": [
      "Squash detection takes a branch whose combined diff shares 80% of changed lines with a commit; a commit that nearly duplicates an unmerged glossed branch would be glossed from it (the note records its sources)",
      "Server-side squashes are carried only by someone who has the original commits locally, usually the author",
      "A squash merge that resolved conflicts or changed much of the code may fall below 80% and need `carry` by hand",
      "Existing repos keep their old hooks until `git gloss init --hooks` is re-run",
      "sync's first run checks the unglossed commits on the remote's branches newer than the oldest glossed commit, which can take a while in a large repo",
      "The archive keeps glossed wip snapshots' files, including anything later removed from them such as a pasted secret, until refs/worktree/gloss/archive is deleted"
